    "q-40199": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40199",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖=17$ and $‖v‖=5$, then what is the smallest possible value of $‖u‖?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}17 & =|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =‖u‖\\cdot (5)+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =5‖u‖+‖u+v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5‖u‖+‖u+v‖ & \\le 5‖u‖+(‖u‖+‖v‖) \\\\  & =5‖u‖+(‖u‖+5) \\\\  & =6‖u‖+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}17 & \\le 6‖u‖+5 \\\\ 12 & \\le 6‖u‖ \\\\ 2 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
